  "body": "The paragraph _Some of the types described below list synonyms for these values. These are to be handled as specified by user agents, but must not be used in documents._ states requirements for `rel` keywords but currently falls on its own alone after a full-page table that separates it from the preceding paragraphs where the spec gives all the other general requirements for `rel` keywords.\n\nSo, that _must not be used in documents_ about synonyms is easy to miss. I know [because I missed it](http://stackoverflow.com/questions/35645360/are-attribute-values-like-contents-glossary-for-rel-attribute-deprecated/35645679#35645679).\n\nSo let’s move it up with the other requirements to help author/developer reader not miss it like I did.\n",
